cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TTB1 in your research or software, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "TTB1: Succinct Threaded Ternary Binary Serialization and SIMD/OpenMP Execution Engine"
version: 0.1.0
doi:10.5281/zenodo.24379185
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "[https://github.com/DRL-233/TTB1-Succinct-Threaded-Ternary-Binary-Serialization-and-SIMD-OpenMP-Execution-Engine](https://github.com/DRL-233/TTB1-Succinct-Threaded-Ternary-Binary-Serialization-and-SIMD-OpenMP-Execution-Engine)"
abstract: >
  TTB1 is a succinct binary wire format (2.60-3.89 bits/node) and load-time
  basic-block fusion compiler for threaded ternary trees. By pairing 5-trit
  degree packing with threaded jump links and SIMD/OpenMP execution, TTB1
  achieves up to 30.8x wire compression and >1,000x faster tree aggregation
  than standard JSON parsing without floating-point or matrix operations.
keywords:
  - succinct data structures
  - ternary tree
  - bytecode compiler
  - basic block fusion
  - SIMD
  - OpenMP
  - zero-copy serialization
  - edge computing
authors:
